Z||000000||batboy||12-03-1999||05:45 PM||||I got a email from a member (maybe a Mike?). My email is screwed up again, they are supposed to be doing some upgrades. Anyway, I'll post my answer here hoping he'll see it.<P>The question was: did I have to cut the face plate of my GM size Pioneer CD player to make it fit right?<P>Yes, I had to trim the corners of the stereo face plate a tiny bit in order for the dash trim plate to fit over it better. Hopefully this pic will show what I mean.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/pioneerinstall.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||superXmotorsports||12-03-1999||07:12 PM||||I had the same or similar Pioneer CD deck in my GTR.  I had trimmed the back of the panel that covers the radio and heater.  (there is a protruding piece on the back on either side.  However Batboy's is probably a better method.||||reg||1
